{#
  FormView branch of _action_post (separate file: form_start / form_end need symfony/form).

  The hidden leaf fields of the FormView (the CSRF token) are printed on every render, whatever their rendered
  flag: one FormView can legitimately render several times (the scaffolds pre-render the 1.x `toolbar` and a host
  `page_header` override renders `actions` again; one CSRF form shared by every row), and form_end alone would
  print them only the first time. Other children render through form_end (first render only). Hidden fields always
  carry a value attribute (2.2), also when it is empty (a hidden `confirm` / marker field that makes a named form
  "submitted"). Symfony only treats a form as submitted when its name is in the request: a POST Action form should be
  named (or carry a hidden field) — see docs/MIGRATING_BUNDLES.md. 2.19 (REQ-TWIG-005): those hidden fields print
  through nowo_ui_form_hidden() — the hidden_widget block of form/nowo_ui_kit_fields.html.twig, same markup — instead
  of a hand-written input.

  The FormView is action_form (2.18, nowo_ui_action_form(): action.form or the CSRF-only form of action.csrfToken),
  else action.form.
#}
{% set _action_form = action_form is defined and action_form is not null ? action_form : action.form %}
{{ form_start(_action_form, {action: action_href ?? '#', method: action.method, attr: {class: 'nowo-ui-action__form'}|merge(form_id|default(null) ? {id: form_id} : {})}) }}
    <button type="submit" class="{{ button_class }}"{% for name, value in button_attrs %}{% if value is same as(true) %} {{ name }}{% elseif value is not null and value is not same as(false) %} {{ name }}="{{ value }}"{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% if action.disabled %} disabled{% endif %}>{{ button_html }}</button>
    {%- for _field in _action_form|filter(f => 'hidden' in f.vars.block_prefixes and f.children is empty) -%}
        {{- nowo_ui_form_hidden(_field) -}}
        {%- do _field.setRendered() -%}
    {%- endfor %}
{{ form_end(_action_form) }}
